@1 = ~You need to know how to play a man. Look around you. You're a beautiful woman surrounded by a bunch of lustful men. You and I both have similar needs, and we need to know how to take care of them. Playing fair won't do you any good. To accomplish victory, you need to wrap them around your finger. Works like a charm.~
@2 = ~Hm. You sound like you're experienced with that. I do see these swines glancing at me when they think I'm not looking. I could use that to my advantage.~
@3 = ~Make them fall in love with your charm and court you. When they do, they'll do anything for you. Woman to woman, men are easy to break if you know where to push them.~
@4 = ~Then I shall give it a try.~
@5 = ~I should warn you, fair lady: some men have rather more wit than their purses would suggest. Mind that you aren't the one being played.~
@6 = ~I'll keep my wits about me, I promise.~
@7 = ~Such a rare sight to see an orc enjoying himself rather than scheming. If only more of them could appreciate the sentiment of culture and trade rather than wage puny wars.~
@8 = ~A fine festival has a way of making friends of strangers. See? Even your stern words almost sound like a compliment, Jaheira.~
@9 = ~Do not test your luck, Coran.~
